WEBVTT

00:00.590 --> 00:02.730
The one who holds the Sun Flower...

00:03.690 --> 00:04.750
- ...is me!
- ...is me!

00:05.730 --> 00:08.150
They are both coming out?

00:08.150 --> 00:09.470
My guess is

00:10.750 --> 00:14.860
that either Master Fay or Lady Leshea
have the Sun Flower,

00:14.860 --> 00:16.700
but the other one has
the Poison Flower.

00:16.700 --> 00:18.460
That's what I think.

00:18.880 --> 00:21.250
Could they both be lying?

00:23.260 --> 00:25.570
Of course, it is possible.

00:29.990 --> 00:33.590
Master Fay, let me see
this through to the end!

00:34.500 --> 00:35.970
What does this mean?

00:35.970 --> 00:37.820
What are they thinking?

00:38.180 --> 00:40.300
Fay, what are you doing?

00:41.840 --> 00:42.650
Fay.

00:43.150 --> 00:45.180
I'll play along with your little game.

00:49.590 --> 00:50.900
This is fine.

00:50.900 --> 00:55.180
If I can't fool my friends,
I can't fool the god.

00:56.080 --> 00:59.040
Sorry to keep you all waiting!

00:59.040 --> 01:00.040
Well, then...

01:00.500 --> 01:03.140
Game start!

01:12.170 --> 01:14.430
Come to me, my army.

01:17.020 --> 01:17.890
What?

01:21.600 --> 01:25.700
Another cat golems!
They're so cute!

01:25.700 --> 01:27.570
No, wait...

01:31.360 --> 01:32.990
Hey, hey, hey!

01:35.280 --> 01:36.950
There are too many of them!

01:37.520 --> 01:39.410
A fine sight.

01:39.410 --> 01:42.980
15 pawns against 1,667 pawns.

01:44.720 --> 01:47.030
A good, fair fight!

01:47.980 --> 01:51.600
How is that fair?!

02:20.450 --> 02:22.120
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

02:23.500 --> 02:28.750
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

03:23.930 --> 03:24.790
SUNSTEAL SCRAMBLE

03:24.790 --> 03:25.750
WIN CONDITION 1:

03:25.750 --> 03:26.620
OFFER THE SUN FLOWER
ON THE HIGHEST LEVEL OF THE PYRAMID

03:26.620 --> 03:27.370
WIN CONDITION 2:

03:27.370 --> 03:27.970
STEAL THE GOD TEAM'S SUN FLOWER

03:27.970 --> 03:28.540
LOSE CONDITION:

03:28.540 --> 03:29.110
THE HUMAN TEAM'S SUN FLOWER IS STOLEN

03:29.730 --> 03:34.650
PLAYER.08: WHERE HAS THE SUN GONE?

03:35.860 --> 03:37.910
I only saw the god and three servants.

03:37.910 --> 03:40.500
And we had 15 players,
including Lady Leoleshea.

03:40.500 --> 03:42.560
I thought it was going
to be an easy win.

03:43.530 --> 03:45.580
But my calculations were wrong!

03:46.800 --> 03:47.940
I'll go first.

03:47.940 --> 03:50.320
Kelritch is too fast!

03:50.750 --> 03:52.380
We can count on her.

03:52.380 --> 03:54.960
And she hadn't even
activated her Arise yet.

03:58.500 --> 04:01.260
Don't you think they're getting faster?

04:04.040 --> 04:05.980
60 km per hour, huh?

04:06.450 --> 04:08.830
They're going to catch up
with us in 30 seconds.

04:08.830 --> 04:10.690
There's no way we can win!

04:10.690 --> 04:14.960
God's army is chasing us
faster than humans.

04:14.960 --> 04:17.780
That was the message of this game:
"Do something about it."

04:17.780 --> 04:19.790
What do you mean by
"do something about it"?

04:20.860 --> 04:22.830
Hey, human up front!
Get out of the way!

04:22.830 --> 04:24.830
Kelritch! Jump back!

04:26.160 --> 04:28.120
It's time for some divine punishment!

04:31.670 --> 04:33.000
A sandstorm?

04:35.960 --> 04:38.660
Does that mean the cat golems
can use ranged magic?

04:38.660 --> 04:40.670
And what is divine punishment?

04:40.670 --> 04:42.460
It's great magic that catches you

04:42.460 --> 04:45.430
if you get too close and penalizes you
if you run too far away.

04:45.430 --> 04:48.890
I don't think a human would stand
a chance against that one.

04:50.690 --> 04:52.650
H-Help me!

04:52.650 --> 04:54.360
Let him go! You monster cat!

05:00.070 --> 05:01.280
Crap!

05:09.960 --> 05:12.880
Don't get carried away! Frostbite!

05:19.300 --> 05:21.890
O God and his armies!
Behold my power!

05:21.890 --> 05:23.390
This is my power!

05:23.390 --> 05:25.210
Dax Hurricane!

05:26.970 --> 05:29.230
Is that really the name
of that technique?

05:29.230 --> 05:31.230
What a beautiful name.

05:32.040 --> 05:33.440
Pearl! Above you!

05:33.440 --> 05:34.270
Huh?

05:36.360 --> 05:38.320
I don't want to be crushed!

05:46.640 --> 05:48.200
The Wondering!

05:49.710 --> 05:51.860
You're not cute at all!

05:51.860 --> 05:52.730
Huh?

05:55.810 --> 05:56.880
Pearl?!

05:59.340 --> 06:03.300
I'm doomed in so many ways!

06:08.580 --> 06:10.330
I hate pervert cat.

06:10.330 --> 06:12.140
Kelritch!

06:19.030 --> 06:22.250
I have a boxing license.

06:22.250 --> 06:24.290
I'm often told
it seems out of character.

06:24.290 --> 06:28.300
Thank you very much!
That is Cosmic Impact, right?!

06:28.300 --> 06:30.770
I don't recall giving it a name like that.

06:30.770 --> 06:32.660
It's called 'Aura Drive.'

06:36.750 --> 06:37.920
Guys!

06:39.780 --> 06:41.760
Their numbers are too many!

06:43.650 --> 06:44.430
Get down!

06:44.430 --> 06:45.430
Huh?

06:45.430 --> 06:48.210
Shatter!

06:56.250 --> 06:57.770
All right, let's move on.

06:59.040 --> 07:03.110
If we make her angry,
is the human world in jeopardy?

07:03.110 --> 07:05.150
Shh! She'll hear you.

07:08.790 --> 07:11.580
The ground is returning to normal!

07:11.580 --> 07:15.540
This is Elements.
The desert can regenerate itself.

07:15.890 --> 07:18.260
So it's all an act of god, huh?

07:19.230 --> 07:20.500
What is that?

07:20.910 --> 07:21.750
A forest?

07:22.490 --> 07:23.280
No.

07:24.510 --> 07:25.750
That's an oasis.

07:26.430 --> 07:29.110
Our goal is the pyramid, but...

07:29.110 --> 07:31.760
This desert has a unique gimmick.

07:32.390 --> 07:35.010
Kelritch, what do you think of that one?

07:35.010 --> 07:37.170
Normally, we should ignore it.

07:37.170 --> 07:40.220
But I think Pearl should go
and change her clothes.

07:40.220 --> 07:41.520
Y-Yes.

07:42.610 --> 07:44.440
I-It's not good!

07:44.440 --> 07:45.890
The golems!

07:48.910 --> 07:51.100
Leshea, can you do that again?

07:51.100 --> 07:52.450
Got it.

08:03.000 --> 08:04.370
No way!

08:04.370 --> 08:06.220
They can fly that far?!

08:06.220 --> 08:07.290
You...!

08:10.640 --> 08:13.350
They have a magic-proof shield?!

08:16.270 --> 08:16.980
You little...!

08:20.970 --> 08:21.730
Camilla!

08:21.730 --> 08:22.860
Stay back!

08:22.860 --> 08:26.820
I have the Sand Flower.
It won't matter if they take it from me!

08:26.820 --> 08:27.810
But...

08:28.450 --> 08:32.070
Go! Freeze, felines!

08:35.490 --> 08:38.210
Don't worry about us! Just go!

08:39.860 --> 08:40.610
Sorry!

08:42.630 --> 08:43.620
600 METERS TO THE PYRAMID

08:43.620 --> 08:45.180
HUMAN'S SIDE: 5 PLAYERS REMAINING

08:45.180 --> 08:46.460
(1 SUN FLOWER, 1 POISON FLOWER,
3 SAND FLOWERS)

08:46.460 --> 08:47.820
GOD'S ARMY: 1237 CREATURES INCLUDING GOD

08:47.820 --> 08:49.130
(1 SUN FLOWER, 1 POISON FLOWER,
1237 SAND FLOWERS)

08:50.090 --> 08:51.090
Dax...

08:51.660 --> 08:53.550
Dax, shouldn't you hide your flower?

08:54.310 --> 08:55.810
If they catch us, we're done.

08:55.810 --> 08:57.810
There's no point in hiding the flower.

08:57.810 --> 09:01.270
Then it's better to keep it in my hand
so I can throw it if the need arises.

09:01.270 --> 09:04.860
If I were you,
I'd run as fast as I could.

09:09.170 --> 09:11.740
Long-range divine punishment!

09:12.950 --> 09:15.790
I won't let that happen!
The Wandering!

09:21.580 --> 09:22.920
Dax!

09:27.660 --> 09:28.690
You...

09:29.340 --> 09:31.090
You damn sand puppets!

09:31.850 --> 09:33.790
Kelritch, calm down!

09:34.700 --> 09:37.200
I have the Sand Flower.

09:37.200 --> 09:41.100
Whoever of you three
has the Sun Flower,

09:41.100 --> 09:43.150
I'll stay here to slow them down.

09:43.150 --> 09:44.860
Quick, get to the pyramid!

09:45.510 --> 09:46.860
I like the way you think.

09:46.860 --> 09:47.870
Huh?

09:48.320 --> 09:51.470
I don't have the Sun Flower either,

09:51.470 --> 09:53.280
so I'll stall them too.

09:54.230 --> 09:55.740
I'm counting on you.

09:56.730 --> 09:57.580
Sure.

10:01.110 --> 10:03.250
My apologies, Chief Secretary.

10:03.250 --> 10:05.510
Not at all. You did well.

10:06.210 --> 10:07.750
Now, let me ask you straightly:

10:08.330 --> 10:10.420
Who has the Sun Flower?

10:10.970 --> 10:12.790
This is just my guess...

10:13.830 --> 10:16.580
As they declared, those two
are holding the Sand Flowers.

10:17.100 --> 10:19.480
I'm guessing that either Fay or Pearl

10:19.480 --> 10:22.820
will be heading for the pyramid
with the Sun Flower or the Poison Flower,

10:22.820 --> 10:25.090
forcing god to choose
between the two.

10:26.090 --> 10:27.250
I see.

10:36.550 --> 10:38.460
Let's make a bet with me,

10:38.950 --> 10:40.740
on the friendly match tomorrow.

10:42.710 --> 10:44.000
Interesting.

10:44.000 --> 10:46.710
I bet Master Fay will win.

10:46.710 --> 10:51.100
If Master Fay wins,
you must do one thing I say.

10:51.100 --> 10:54.490
If you win, I'll join your team.

10:55.310 --> 10:57.240
You won that bet

10:57.870 --> 11:01.560
and demanded that I do everything
in my power to help Fay win.

11:02.290 --> 11:04.220
If he loses, that's the end.

11:07.050 --> 11:08.520
Just watch.

11:08.520 --> 11:11.070
Let's see the play of the man you chose.

11:13.940 --> 11:17.500
We're here!

11:21.990 --> 11:25.000
GODS' GAME WE PLAY

11:26.390 --> 11:27.200
Pearl.

11:28.560 --> 11:30.420
This is Sun Flower.

11:30.940 --> 11:33.510
If we offer it on the altar
at the top of the pyramid,

11:34.320 --> 11:35.700
we will win.

11:36.220 --> 11:40.300
Yes! I'll do my best to support you, Fay!

11:42.210 --> 11:44.020
Well done for making it this far.

11:44.550 --> 11:46.890
All that remains is this slope.

11:46.890 --> 11:49.440
Show me how you will ascend this path!

11:50.020 --> 11:53.390
Let's go, Pearl! We'll run up
to the top step at once!

11:53.390 --> 11:54.530
Yes!

11:54.530 --> 11:56.310
Come to me, my army.

11:58.450 --> 11:59.700
Let's get hurry, Pearl!

12:06.990 --> 12:07.830
Fay!

12:07.830 --> 12:10.790
Don't worry about me!
Keep moving!

12:13.880 --> 12:15.190
The Sun?!

12:15.710 --> 12:17.220
Run, Pearl!

12:20.180 --> 12:21.640
Catch her!

12:35.010 --> 12:36.400
This is perfect!

12:36.400 --> 12:38.480
You think you can surpass me?

12:38.860 --> 12:41.450
If I don't surpass you,
I can't go to the top!

12:44.330 --> 12:45.850
You are in the divine presence!

12:46.650 --> 12:48.170
The Wandering!

12:49.120 --> 12:52.880
Oh? You've moved all the way
to the top of the pyramid.

12:54.750 --> 12:56.310
Where did she disappear?

12:56.310 --> 12:57.320
Over here!

12:58.220 --> 13:00.680
There are two conditions
for victory on the human's team!

13:00.680 --> 13:01.580
WIN CONDITION 1:

13:01.580 --> 13:02.650
OFFER THE SUN FLOWER
ON THE HIGHEST LEVEL OF THE PYRAMID

13:02.650 --> 13:03.250
WIN CONDITION 2:

13:03.250 --> 13:04.640
STEAL THE GOD TEAM'S SUN FLOWER

13:05.360 --> 13:08.390
If we get that flower,
victory is ours!

13:17.860 --> 13:21.840
I did it! I took the flower from god!

13:23.010 --> 13:23.780
Huh?

13:27.020 --> 13:30.330
That's Poison Flower.
You'll be stunned for five seconds.

13:30.330 --> 13:32.330
H-How...?

13:32.940 --> 13:35.840
You humans staked your
hopes on the belief

13:35.840 --> 13:38.780
that I have the Sun Flower, right?

13:39.840 --> 13:42.140
I will show you where my Sun Flower is

13:42.140 --> 13:44.390
as a special act of favor.

13:45.550 --> 13:46.890
Could it be...!

13:48.070 --> 13:51.350
If you want to hide a tree,
it should be in the forest.

13:51.350 --> 13:54.050
Now, the effect of the Poison Flower

13:54.050 --> 13:57.410
will reveal the location of your Sun Flower.

13:57.810 --> 14:01.670
Not that it could be
with anyone but you.

14:02.780 --> 14:07.120
If it were a Poison Flower, it would
have been a little more interesting.

14:08.050 --> 14:10.510
This game is finished...

14:12.580 --> 14:13.140
What?

14:13.140 --> 14:14.580
Huh? Why?

14:19.190 --> 14:21.470
They don't have the Sun Flower either?

14:22.240 --> 14:24.780
The one who holds the Sun Flower...

14:25.250 --> 14:26.100
- ...is me!
- ...is me!

14:30.610 --> 14:33.260
No one had the Sun Flower, you say?!

14:34.050 --> 14:36.140
Where has the sun gone?!

14:37.390 --> 14:39.140
It's time to compare answers.

14:40.100 --> 14:40.950
O' god!

14:42.500 --> 14:45.530
I've had two flowers all along.

14:46.810 --> 14:52.200
There was one apostle who went out without
losing his flowers to the cat golem, right?

15:00.560 --> 15:03.590
The one who had the sun flower is Dax?!

15:04.240 --> 15:07.690
In the first place,
Dax was running in the lead

15:07.690 --> 15:10.170
because he was further away
from the cat golem,

15:10.170 --> 15:13.730
deliberately going over the distance
to get caught in that sandstorm.

15:14.420 --> 15:16.340
By being engulfed by that sandstorm,

15:16.340 --> 15:18.980
he hid the moment
when he threw the Sun Flower.

15:20.880 --> 15:24.220
The gods smile at those
who make their own miracles.

15:24.990 --> 15:28.120
How about it? It turned out
to be a fun game, didn't it?

15:29.520 --> 15:30.690
Delightful!

15:31.340 --> 15:34.560
Let's see if you can surpass the path
to the sun that stands before you!

15:35.300 --> 15:37.040
Come to me, my army.

15:38.080 --> 15:40.500
What? A five-second stun?!

15:41.130 --> 15:44.460
As soon as you knew that Fay and Pearl
didn't have the Poison Flower,

15:44.460 --> 15:48.390
you should have stopped your troops.

15:52.510 --> 15:55.230
I was the one who had
the Poison Flower!

15:57.230 --> 16:01.660
'The flowers must not be taken from us.'
It's a reversal of that idea.

16:01.660 --> 16:03.690
By using the force of the flower,

16:04.110 --> 16:06.650
we can stun the god for five seconds!

16:07.040 --> 16:09.410
But five seconds...

16:09.410 --> 16:13.100
You forgot the most important thing, god.

16:15.350 --> 16:19.840
I'm just an insignificant human
from your perspective.

16:21.100 --> 16:24.420
Throwing him on the altar
is not a problem for me.

16:26.830 --> 16:30.180
I'm a little jealous of you.

16:31.890 --> 16:35.220
Dax's heart has always been glued to you.

16:35.830 --> 16:38.640
So this is my way
of working off some steam!

16:43.770 --> 16:47.190
Ouch! You actually hit me, didn't you?!

16:47.190 --> 16:48.510
Unbelievable...

16:57.210 --> 17:01.040
Well, the point is,
we won this together.

17:03.530 --> 17:04.880
I have no objection.

17:09.020 --> 17:11.620
There is no end to the games
between humans and the gods.

17:12.170 --> 17:15.930
I'll be waiting for you in another game.

17:16.430 --> 17:17.730
I look forward to it.

17:18.390 --> 17:21.730
Therefore, I leave that flower to you.

17:24.150 --> 17:25.660
VS MAHTMA II, THE GOD OF THE SUN ARMY
SUNSTEAL SCRAMBLE

17:25.660 --> 17:27.150
TIME ELAPSED: 54 MINUTES, 19 SECONDS
WIN

17:27.150 --> 17:28.460
DROPPED ITEM: SUN FLOWER
DROPPED ON DIFFICULTY: MYTHIC

17:28.460 --> 17:30.410
THIS FLOWER IS SAID TO HAVE THE POWER
TO SUMMON THE SUN,

17:30.410 --> 17:32.860
BUT EXACTLY WHAT THAT MEANS IS UNKNOWN

17:39.600 --> 17:40.710
I've heard about it.

17:40.710 --> 17:43.810
You made a bet with Dax
and got him to give it his all

17:43.810 --> 17:45.490
so that I would win, right?

17:45.970 --> 17:46.920
Thank you.

17:46.920 --> 17:48.010
No...

17:48.010 --> 17:51.370
I just wanted to see you win.

17:53.820 --> 17:55.600
Is that all you really wanted?

17:59.220 --> 18:00.580
I...

18:02.170 --> 18:04.650
What I really want is to challenge
the gods' game

18:04.650 --> 18:06.440
with you as an apostle

18:07.100 --> 18:09.400
on the same team!

18:10.180 --> 18:11.450
Let's do it, then.

18:12.260 --> 18:14.360
But I had already lost three times!

18:15.230 --> 18:17.340
I have no choice but to retire...

18:17.340 --> 18:18.330
No.

18:18.330 --> 18:19.950
There is still a way.

18:20.540 --> 18:21.540
Right?

18:22.300 --> 18:27.300
Sir Fay, what you're thinking
carries the greatest risk.

18:27.820 --> 18:32.260
And no one in the world has even
attempted it in at least 20 years.

18:32.260 --> 18:33.730
20 years?!

18:34.450 --> 18:36.110
I'm aware of that.

18:36.110 --> 18:38.620
What's your record, Nel?

18:38.620 --> 18:41.220
Uh, three wins and three losses.

18:41.220 --> 18:42.900
I see.

18:47.330 --> 18:49.190
I think I can make this work.

18:50.130 --> 18:53.700
Secretary Baleggar, could you get in touch
with Chief Secretary Miranda for me?

18:54.370 --> 18:57.220
We're going to face the Bookmaker.

18:59.690 --> 19:03.040
Yes, there is a god called 'Bookmaker.'

19:03.370 --> 19:04.600
ORDINARY GODS
With an ordinary god, if you win,

19:04.600 --> 19:06.040
ORDINARY GODS
you are granted one win.

19:06.040 --> 19:07.630
BOOKMAKER
But Bookmaker

19:07.630 --> 19:09.600
2 WIN 2 LOSE - 2 WIN 2 LOSE
does not increase the number of wins

19:09.600 --> 19:11.840
3 WIN 2 LOSE - 2 WIN 1 LOSE
but decreases the number of losses.

19:12.310 --> 19:16.900
But you can only dive into the Bookmaker
through a certain Divine Gate.

19:16.900 --> 19:20.310
Unfortunately, the Mal-ra branch
doesn't seem to have one.

19:20.310 --> 19:22.770
But we have it in Ruin, right?

19:24.350 --> 19:28.560
Well, at our place, it's a Divine Gate that's
been buried in dust for about 40 years.

19:28.960 --> 19:30.980
So, how do you challenge it?

19:30.980 --> 19:34.690
Nel will use my one win
to challenge the Bookmaker.

19:35.040 --> 19:38.780
If we win, one of Nel's losses will go away,
and she will get back to two losses.

19:38.780 --> 19:41.440
But using Fay's one win means...

19:41.440 --> 19:42.620
Wait a minute!

19:42.620 --> 19:46.250
If you lose your one win
by betting on me...

19:46.250 --> 19:47.810
I don't mind it.

19:47.810 --> 19:48.710
No.

19:49.210 --> 19:51.070
Fay has won six games.

19:51.070 --> 19:53.670
He's on track to win 10 games
for the first time in history,

19:53.670 --> 19:56.700
so betting on his one win is a big problem.

19:57.330 --> 20:00.020
Then she can wager one of my wins!

20:00.760 --> 20:03.940
It's true that Fay's one win
is too important.

20:03.940 --> 20:06.730
Then betting on my one win
is the only solution!

20:08.440 --> 20:12.540
Nel really wants to play
the game with us.

20:12.540 --> 20:15.180
We feel the same way.

20:15.180 --> 20:16.400
Isn't that right?

20:16.710 --> 20:17.650
That's right.

20:17.650 --> 20:21.650
That's what we decided.
You have to agree with us, Chief Secretary.

20:21.650 --> 20:24.930
And I still want to bet on my winnings.

20:24.930 --> 20:26.370
Is that cool with you, Leshea?

20:26.740 --> 20:28.500
Yeah, I don't mind.

20:29.180 --> 20:30.450
Say, Miranda.

20:30.450 --> 20:32.090
Yes, Lady Leoleshea?

20:32.630 --> 20:35.480
Speaking as a former deity myself,

20:35.480 --> 20:39.050
I can tell you that I really don't care about
apostles who want to make a comeback.

20:39.050 --> 20:40.570
You know...

20:41.360 --> 20:44.760
The gods only smile on those
who make their own miracles.

20:45.350 --> 20:49.230
At least Fay is trying to help
one person, which is Nel.

20:49.690 --> 20:52.230
I think that makes her worth a look.

20:52.230 --> 20:53.690
I guess that settles it.

20:55.270 --> 20:57.790
Well, as soon as you get back to Ruin,

20:57.790 --> 21:00.030
I'll get things in order.

21:02.230 --> 21:03.100
Everyone...

21:08.460 --> 21:10.740
A miracle hasn't happened yet.

21:10.740 --> 21:14.420
All we can do is get
the miraculous pins lined up.

21:15.100 --> 21:16.670
You must win this one, Nel.

21:16.670 --> 21:19.630
Yes, of course!
Thank you.

21:19.630 --> 21:21.340
Master Fay, Pearl,

21:21.340 --> 21:22.810
and Lady Leoleshea.

21:23.740 --> 21:25.630
I can't thank any of you enough!

21:27.270 --> 21:29.370
Even the Chief Secretary said like that,

21:29.370 --> 21:32.030
don't worry about betting on my wins.

21:32.030 --> 21:33.210
Even if you lose a game or—

21:33.210 --> 21:34.610
Absolutely not!

21:35.530 --> 21:38.010
I'll borrow only one win
from you, Master Fay.

21:38.010 --> 21:41.460
That's all I need to win
against the Bookmaker!

21:42.990 --> 21:47.620
96 HOURS LATER

21:52.140 --> 21:53.580
How boring.

21:54.170 --> 21:56.360
You're way too weak.

21:56.360 --> 21:58.260
N-No way...
